[0.007816, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ claude\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m> PROMPT:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.009716, "o", "  Read CLAUDE.md. Build the matching engine and the core UI.\r\n  \r\n  1. src/lib/grades.js — toGPA(input, scale) supporting: 4.0-scale number, percentage 0–100, letter grades A+ through D. Export GRADE_OPTIONS for the UI.\r\n  2. src/lib/match.js — implement matchScore + labels exactly as CLAUDE.md specifies. Export matchUniversities(profile, universities) returning sorted results with { university, score, label, gpaGap }.\r\n  3. ProfileForm component — grade input with a scale selector (GPA / Percentage / Letter), interest picker as toggleable chips (canonical tags), and a prominent \"Find my matches\" button.\r\n  4. ResultsGrid + UniversityCard — card shows name, city+country flag emoji, match score as an animated ring or bar, Safety/Match/Reach badge (color-coded: green/indigo/amber), field tags, tuition + living + application fee, ranking band, website link.\r\n  5. StatsBar above results: total matches, count by label, cheapest option, best-fit country.\r\n  6. Wire it all in App.jsx with useState/useMemo. Empty state before first search: friendly illustration made of CSS, short copy.\r\n  7. `npm run build` must pass. Also add 8 unit-style assertions in scripts/test-match.mjs (plain node asserts) covering grade conversion and labeling, add \"test\" script, and make them pass.\r\n"]
[0.009935, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- Claude Code session start ---\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[293.488877, "o", "All pieces are built and verified. Summary:\r\n\r\n**Built:**\r\n- `src/lib/grades.js` — `toGPA(input, scale)` for GPA/percentage/letter, `GRADE_OPTIONS` + `LETTER_GRADE_OPTIONS` for the UI\r\n- `src/lib/match.js` — `matchUniversities(profile, universities)`: academic fit (60%, full credit at/above minGPA, linear down to 0 at −0.4), interest fit (40%, tag overlap), Safety/Match/Reach labeling, sorted by score\r\n- `src/lib/countryFlags.js` — country → flag emoji helper\r\n- `ProfileForm` — scale selector, grade input (number or letter dropdown depending on scale), toggleable interest chips, \"Find my matches\" button\r\n- `UniversityCard` + `ResultsGrid` — animated SVG score ring, color-coded badge, field chips, tuition/living/fee/total costs, ranking, website link, CSS-only empty state and \"no results\" state\r\n- `StatsBar` — total matches, per-label counts, cheapest option, best-fit country (by avg score)\r\n- `FilterBar` — region chips, country chips, tuition/total-cost sliders, reach-schools toggle\r\n- `App.jsx` — wired with `useState`/`useMemo` only, filters applied after matching\r\n\r\n**Verified:**\r\n- `npm run build` passes (Vite production build, 43 modules)\r\n- `npm run test` runs `scripts/test-match.mjs` with 8 assertions (grade conversion for all three scales + Safety/Match/Reach labeling) — all pass\r\n- Spot-checked grade conversion values directly in node\r\n\r\n**Not verified:** I couldn't get a live browser check — this sandbox blocks backgrounding the dev server (`&`) even with `nohup`/`disown`, so I couldn't view the running app in Chrome. Confidence comes from the passing build/tests and manual review of prop wiring across components, not an actual rendered check. If you want, I can try again with dev-server permissions unblocked, or you can run `npm run dev` locally to eyeball it.\r\n"]
[293.757707, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- session complete (exit 0) ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
